$ secskills scope --validate
[stderr]
error: cannot read .secskills-scope.yml: open .secskills-scope.yml: no such file or directory
[exit 1]

$ secskills scope --init
wrote .secskills-scope.yml — edit it, set authorized: true after you have written authorization.
[exit 0]

# file <SANDBOX>/cwd/.secskills-scope.yml
# secskills engagement scope — written by intake, honored by the authorization gate
engagement: <name>
authorized: false          # set true ONLY with written authorization from the target owner
engagement_type: black-box # black-box | grey-box | white-box
confirmed_by: <you@org>
expires: <TIME>
intrusive: false           # true requires a second explicit confirmation at test time
targets:
  - <apex-domain>
out_of_scope:
  - <host-to-exclude>

# end

$ secskills scope --validate
scope file: .secskills-scope.yml
  authorized: false · type: black-box · intrusive: false
  expires: <TIME> (valid)
  targets: <apex-domain>
  out_of_scope: <host-to-exclude>
  RESULT: NOT authorized — discover/test will require --confirm until authorized: true.
[exit 0]

